WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.630
- I've visited over 125 countries,

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.510
and I've been to all seven
continents of the world.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.150
Old Town, Jerusalem.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.250
Yet I've seen nothing.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.150
My name's Tony Giles.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.150
I'm totally blind,

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.403
severely deaf, yet, I
travel the world alone.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.003
I come from Southwest England.

00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:25.970
I was born with a rare eye condition.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.240
I could see shapes and shadows.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.460
I was very light-sensitive as a child,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.472
but by the time I was eight, nine,

00:00:31.472 --> 00:00:33.630
my light sensitivity would go.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.851
When I was 16, I got the opportunity

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:35.741
to go to the States,

00:00:35.741 --> 00:00:36.720
and I was all excited,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.463
and that's what I really loved:

00:00:38.463 --> 00:00:39.296
I loved the adventure

00:00:39.296 --> 00:00:40.291
and the unknown.

00:00:40.291 --> 00:00:43.352
I thought, "Wow, I'm gonna
travel for the rest of my life

00:00:43.352 --> 00:00:45.371
"and see if I can visit
every country in the world."

00:00:45.371 --> 00:00:47.580
So I thought I needed to take photos,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.960
so I’ve got actual evidence that I've been there.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.541
And I also think it's quite fun, you know,

00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:53.160
the general public to see a blind person

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.410
taking photos, that must look like a

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.392
mess with their heads.

00:00:56.392 --> 00:00:58.381
I find that quite interesting.

00:00:58.381 --> 00:01:00.541
People think, "How can you
travel when you're blind

00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:04.660
"and how can you visit
all these countries?"

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.620
I got a series of
different maps on my walls,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:07.460
so I've got an idea

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.833
of what each country I'm visiting looks like.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.730
I research the country I visit,

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.507
so I get on the Internet.

00:01:16.507 --> 00:01:20.090
- [Computerized Voice] L-E-B-A-N-O-N.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.177
- [Tony] One British pound equals?

00:01:21.177 --> 00:01:24.480
- [Computerized Voice]
Lebanese 2001 (mumbles)

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.313
- And then I look up each city and

00:01:25.313 --> 00:01:26.820
what I want to visit.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.810
Is it museums or churches or mosques?

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:31.136
I try and find places with audio guides.

00:01:31.136 --> 00:01:33.917
And in terms of visits, obviously, as a blind person,

00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:35.625
I'm not going
to go and see a country.

00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:37.885
I'm not interested in looking
at the beautiful vistas.

00:01:37.885 --> 00:01:39.621
So I need to walk places,

00:01:39.621 --> 00:01:42.520
I need to feel the
atmosphere, touch things.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.833
I rely on people
everywhere I go to help me.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:49.510
A lot of countries I visit, obviously,

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.760
English isn't their first language.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.360
So, for instance, I'll ask the,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.810
the staff to write down in Arabic

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.290
the places I want to go.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.670
I meet people on the street,

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:58.580
and they give me directions

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.180
or they help me to go to places.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.317
People ask me, "Are all
the places you've been

00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:06.530
"in the same because you can't see them?"

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.710
And every city, every town,
every country is different.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.046
The thing I love about it most is moving

00:02:11.046 --> 00:02:12.166
and actually getting

00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:15.840
from one place to another, that challenge.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.056
So once you actually sort of reach,

00:02:17.056 --> 00:02:18.926
reach the destination or the
place you're looking for,

00:02:18.926 --> 00:02:21.090
that's a huge achievement.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.347
Yeah, that's why I do it.

00:02:22.347 --> 00:02:25.257
That's--
That's the ultimate reason

00:02:25.257 --> 00:02:27.257
for my travels, really.

